WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.540
Every year, India's government

2
00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:04.320
must ask Parliament for

3
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.940
permission to spend.

4
00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:08.430
The asking has a calendar.

5
00:00:08.883 --> 00:00:10.693
First, the estimates.

6
00:00:11.423 --> 00:00:13.603
About five to six months before

7
00:00:13.603 --> 00:00:15.863
the Budget, a Finance Ministry

8
00:00:15.863 --> 00:00:18.223
circular asks every ministry for

9
00:00:18.223 --> 00:00:20.163
its figures, rather like a

10
00:00:20.163 --> 00:00:22.063
wedding planner asking relatives

11
00:00:22.063 --> 00:00:23.953
how many will really come.

12
00:00:24.404 --> 00:00:25.424
Then the Budget.

13
00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:27.704
Article one hundred twelve:

14
00:00:27.704 --> 00:00:30.984
a yearly statement of receipts

15
00:00:30.984 --> 00:00:31.784
and spending.

16
00:00:31.784 --> 00:00:34.744
Since twenty seventeen, it

17
00:00:34.744 --> 00:00:36.004
arrives on the first of

18
00:00:36.004 --> 00:00:37.034
February.

19
00:00:37.384 --> 00:00:39.544
Next, discussion.

20
00:00:39.544 --> 00:00:41.584
Both Houses debate the whole

21
00:00:41.584 --> 00:00:43.864
Budget, with no vote.

22
00:00:43.864 --> 00:00:46.144
Standing committees study each

23
00:00:46.144 --> 00:00:47.714
ministry's demands.

24
00:00:48.213 --> 00:00:50.493
Now, the vote.

25
00:00:50.493 --> 00:00:53.513
Article one hundred thirteen:

26
00:00:53.513 --> 00:00:55.813
demands for grants go to the Lok

27
00:00:55.813 --> 00:00:56.883
Sabha alone.

28
00:00:57.553 --> 00:00:59.413
The Rajya Sabha may discuss

29
00:00:59.413 --> 00:01:01.693
them, like a commentator with no

30
00:01:01.693 --> 00:01:02.493
bat.

31
00:01:02.855 --> 00:01:05.435
Then, the Appropriation Bill.

32
00:01:05.435 --> 00:01:07.615
Article one hundred fourteen:

33
00:01:07.615 --> 00:01:09.935
no money leaves the Consolidated

34
00:01:09.935 --> 00:01:12.215
Fund except by law.

35
00:01:12.215 --> 00:01:14.775
The Finance Bill follows, for

36
00:01:14.775 --> 00:01:15.645
taxes.

37
00:01:16.178 --> 00:01:17.618
The first of April.

38
00:01:17.618 --> 00:01:19.978
The new year begins.

39
00:01:19.978 --> 00:01:22.838
If money runs short, Article one

40
00:01:22.838 --> 00:01:24.758
hundred fifteen allows a

41
00:01:24.758 --> 00:01:26.268
supplementary statement.

42
00:01:27.462 --> 00:01:28.062
For GS3:

43
00:01:28.062 --> 00:01:30.382
Articles one hundred twelve to

44
00:01:30.382 --> 00:01:31.442
one hundred sixteen.

45
00:01:31.442 --> 00:01:34.482
The Lok Sabha votes the grants,

46
00:01:34.482 --> 00:01:37.192
and money moves only by law.

47
00:01:37.925 --> 00:01:40.885
A year of asking, and not a

48
00:01:40.885 --> 00:01:42.695
rupee without a law.
